<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A = {\{2, 5, 8, 11, 14\}}</m> and <m>B = {\{\text{the even numbers between 5 and 15}\}}</m>.</p><p>(a) List the elements of <m>A \cup B</m>.</p><p><fillin characters="25" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) List the elements of <m>A \cap B</m>.</p><p><fillin characters="25" name="ans2"/>  </p><p>(c) Find <m>n(A \cup B)</m>.</p><p><fillin characters="5" name="ans3"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>First list <m>B</m>: <m>B = {\{6, 8, 10, 12, 14\}}</m>.</p><p>(a) <m>A \cup B</m> holds the elements in <m>A</m> or <m>B</m> or both, each written once: <m>A \cup B = {\{2, 5, 6, 8, 10, 11, 12, 14\}}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>A \cap B</m> holds the elements in both sets: <m>A \cap B = {\{8, 14\}}</m>.</p><p>(c) <m>n(A \cup B) = {8}</m>. Check: <m>n(A) + n(B) - n(A \cap B) = {10} - {2} = {8}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left \{2 , 5 , 6 , 8 , 10 , 11 , 12 , 14 \right \}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left \{8 , 14 \right \}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>8</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>